  "details": "as to\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/avatar-30/p/feedback-parameter-driver-over-time\n\ni was thinking of extra options aswell.\n\nDelay:\n\nChooses the delay in an animation from 0 to 100% when a driver will start.\n\n(as to post link above:)\n\nSmoothing:\n\nChooses two numbers and blends them together over the course of the animation clip.\n\nAdditive Loop:\n\nChoose a number which adds constantly every frame until the clip ends, a state exit, or a set end value has been met (ex: end looping additive at 0.15 float value)\n\nAdditive loop part 2 (Delay):\n\njust sets a delay between each additive during the clip, default is 0.1\n\nthe Additive Loop and Smoothing will prevent having to use an entire other layer for transitioning values smoothly\n\nSmoothing and Additive Loop are different types, for the exact same situation you'd prefer Add instead of Set\n\nDelay will allow less complicated delay systems for parameter driver updating",
